From: MediaBox
Subject: register the MediaBox video plane output

The appliance's interface is one process that holds DRM master and scans its
own surface out on Cluster0, the primary window of video port 0. There is no
compositor under it any more, so mpv's dmabuf-wayland output has nothing to
draw on -- it is what this player used before, and it exits 2 without one --
and vo_drm would have to take the television away from the interface to get a
picture, which is the thing having our own player was supposed to stop.

video/out/vo_mediabox.c is the third answer: the decoded frame's dma-buf
descriptors go to the interface over a unix socket, and the interface puts them
on the same video port's second window (Esmart0, which takes NV12 and NV15 and
has its own scaler). This is the two lines that make the build know about it.
--- /var/tmp/vo.c.orig
+++ video/out/vo.c
@@ -66,6 +66,7 @@
 extern const struct vo_driver video_out_tct;
 extern const struct vo_driver video_out_sixel;
 extern const struct vo_driver video_out_kitty;
+extern const struct vo_driver video_out_mediabox;
 
 static const struct vo_driver *const video_out_drivers[] =
 {
@@ -94,6 +95,12 @@
 #if HAVE_DMABUF_WAYLAND
     &video_out_dmabuf_wayland,
 #endif
+    /* MediaBox's own: hand the decoded frame to the interface that holds DRM
+     * master and let the display controller's second window show it. This
+     * appliance has no compositor, so dmabuf-wayland above has nothing to draw
+     * on and vo_drm below would have to take the television away from the
+     * interface to get it. */
+    &video_out_mediabox,
 #if HAVE_VAAPI_X11 && HAVE_GPL
     &video_out_vaapi,
 #endif
--- /var/tmp/meson.build.orig
+++ meson.build
@@ -243,6 +243,7 @@
     'video/out/vo_image.c',
     'video/out/vo_lavc.c',
     'video/out/vo_libmpv.c',
+    'video/out/vo_mediabox.c',
     'video/out/vo_null.c',
     'video/out/vo_tct.c',
     'video/out/vo_kitty.c',
